# ratchet-baseline, T6's record. tools/check-release.sh reads it as check 10.
#
# The owner set ceilings, not a ratchet. A release may grow. The gate fails only when the words in
# skills/parvis-core/SKILL.md or in all skills/*/SKILL.md together pass the ceiling below. Only the
# owner raises a ceiling, by editing this line.
#
#   ceiling <words in parvis-core/SKILL.md> <words in all skills/*/SKILL.md together>
#
# The owner's reasoning, 2026-09-21. A session loads about 7,650 words, and the whole system is
# about 108,000, against a context of a million tokens, so capacity is not the constraint. What the
# reviews caught was contradiction and drift between copies, which the one-source rule and the
# gate's other checks address. The ceilings sit about 55 percent above the 2.7 measurement.
ceiling 5000 65000
#
# Measurement history, one row per release, by wc -w. It informs and never fails a release.
#
#   release <X.Y> <core words> <always-loaded words>
#
# This is not the VERSION file, which install.sh reads as the bare release string.
release 2.7 3203 41960
